<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Engen half yr shr rises, div unchanged.</title>
<headline>Engen half yr shr rises, div unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended Feb 28, 1996</p>
<p>(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     107.0	 vs 88.0</p>
<p>    Pre-excep shr (cts)   107.0	 vs 84.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 36.0	  vs same</p>
<p>    Net income		191.0	 vs 140.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   237.0	 vs 170.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 53.0	  vs 30.0</p>
<p>    Net finance expense   51.0	  vs 79.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     none	  vs 8.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  6,099.0     vs 4,584.0</p>
<p>Div payable May 28</p>
<p>on register April 25</p>
<p>Full name: Engen Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll of analysts forecast earnings for the half year to February 28 rising to between 90 cents and 108 cents with consensus at 103.2 cents.</p>
<p>The first half dividend was seen rising to within a range of 36 and 50 cents with consensus at 44 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
